# validator_missing_body_test.deor
# Exercises check_validator_declaration's missing-predicate-body check. Before this
# check existed, a validator type declared with no indented body didn't just fail to
# validate — depending on where it sat in the file it could panic the transpiler
# process itself with an internal index-out-of-bounds error (reading past the header's
# NEWLINE into whatever followed, or off the end of the token stream entirely) instead
# of reporting a clean error. Covers a mid-file case (followed by another declaration)
# and an end-of-file case (nothing at all follows the header) — the two failure shapes
# the original crash depended on.

type Empty1(int val)

type Empty2(int val)

fn void main()
	print("unreachable")

# expect-error:
# line 11: type 'Empty1' - validator type is missing a predicate body
# line 13: type 'Empty2' - validator type is missing a predicate body
